    "questionText": "Two situations are contrasted in a physiology tutorial. In the first, a single lung segment is poorly ventilated while the remainder of the lung is normal. In the second, every alveolus in both lungs is exposed to a low oxygen tension simultaneously. Which of the following best distinguishes the consequences of these two situations for pulmonary vascular resistance?",
